  "conclusion": "Three independent stages \u2014 orbit discrepancy mod 3^n, 2D Weyl discrepancy of (a log 2 - b log 3) mod 1, and the Markoff-orbit cross-check \u2014 all show the (2,3)-system has *exactly* the well-distribution / mixing that classical Baker / Weyl theory predicts, with no measurable surplus mixing that sum-product machinery could exploit. The orbit of 2 mod 3^n is moreover structurally rigid (LTE), making it a poor candidate for a sum-product argument."
